571 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 216 0 R
/T <4D656E746F7290732072656C6174696F6E736869702073746F7279>
/E <4D656E746F7290732072656C6174696F6E736869702073746F7279>
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
572 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/ActualText ("Before coming to Saigon, I felt incredibly lonely. Not because I couldn't connect with anyone, but because no one seemed to have enough time or patience to listen. If you were to ask me if I was okay, I wasn't really. So, I decided to go elsewhere for study and work, or as some might say, 'run away.' However, arriving in a new city is like starting relationships from ground zero.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
573 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/ActualText (Sure, I had colleagues, but when it came to a truly connected relationship, I had none. At that time, all my relationships were more of a social nature rather than being intimate enough to share deeply.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
574 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/ActualText (It may sound dreadful, doesn't it? However, living without friends isn't as bad as we might think.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
575 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/ActualText (Later on, that challenging period helped me realize what a true friend should be like. Not everyone will accompany us in our journey, and even if they do, they may leave us at some point. In other words, the only constant companion we have is ourselves. Even family members have their own paths and can't accompany us throughout life. Of course, it's fortunate to have friends, but not having them doesn't mean you're inadequate. No one is entirely good or bad. Some people don't have friends due to their introverted nature.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/ActualText (I believe that all of us go through such feelings at times. As someone who has overcome these difficult stages, I am here ready to listen to you...")
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
